{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787111565,"nonce":"F3FOSy0D8h13cJl5YZ1rwoYp79g=","message":"CLOSING AS ALREADY-ADDRESSED, AND FLAGGING THAT THIS TICKET'S PREMISE IS WRONG. Reopen if you disagree — the evidence is below, not a judgement call I want to hide.\n\n**The ticket says ADR 0040 §6 'records the question as undecided'. It records the opposite.** §6, verbatim:\n\n\u003e `refire_grace` no longer decides a transition, **and the setting stays — under its own name, in `orgs.settings`, with its bounds unchanged.** That is the decision, not a deferral. […] Renaming, re-homing and removal are all refused: deleting or moving a settings key is a contract change of its own, and there is nothing to buy by paying it — the question this setting used to answer […] belongs at **case formation**, not at the lifecycle boundary, so the knob for it would be a new key with new semantics rather than this one wearing a new label.\n\nSPEC:232 agrees: \"`refire_grace` therefore no longer decides any transition, and ADR 0040 §6 decides its fate\".\n\n**Clause by clause:**\n\n1. *\"`refire_grace` is gone from the settings contract\"* — this is the thing §6 explicitly refuses. NOT DONE, deliberately.\n2. *\"`group_close_delay_s`'s pinning no longer references it\"* — §6 states that pin as deliberate and live: `DefaultGroupCloseDelay` is pinned at or above `DefaultRefireGrace`, held by `TestGroupCloseDelayDoesNotDefeatTheRefireGrace`. A second pin — the floor at `2 x DedupTTL` — is held by `TestTheReplayWindowIsStrictlyInsideRefireGrace`. Both tests exist (`internal/identity/domain/`). Removing the key unpins BOTH.\n3. *\"No operator-visible copy describes a grace window reopening a case\"* — **ALREADY SATISFIED.** `tuningCopy.ts:379` now reads \"This window no longer decides what happens to that alert: a case is terminal … **Nothing reopens a closed case.** What the number still does is bound two others\". That is exactly the wording §6 mandates. The ticket cites `:352,360`; the content moved and was fixed.\n4. *\"ADR 0040 §6 is amended from 'undecided' to the decision\"* — there is nothing to amend; §6 already says \"That is the decision, not a deferral.\"\n\n**So the only live defect this ticket named — false operator copy — is fixed, and the rest would reverse a recorded decision on a mistaken reading of it.** Executing done-when 1 would have been a 61-file contract change (SEEN, excluding docs-site and node_modules) that unpinned two invariants each protected by a named test.\n\nIf the intent really is to remove the key, that is a decision to take against §6 explicitly, with the two pins re-homed first — not something to reach by following this ticket.\n\nClosed by the AFK orchestrator session on the owner's instruction to work and close the queue.","files":null}]}